Subject: The collection threshold moves only with collections, and starts at 16 MB

What this does
  - quickjs.c js_trigger_gc_slow: when a reconcile alone brings the heap under the threshold, the threshold is left alone (0513 raised it to 1.5x the current size).
  - quickjs.c js_new_runtime: the initial threshold is 16 MB instead of 256 KB.

Why we need it
  The reconcile frees the nursery's dead cells in bulk, so the heap looks small right after it while cyclic garbage keeps growing underneath. Resetting the threshold to 1.5x the post-reconcile size on every such event made it follow the garbage: on deltablue the threshold reached 1.1 GB, every allocation-path call was judged "reconcile enough", and the only collections were at teardown. The threshold is now set only by a collection (post-collection size plus max(16 MB, 50%)), so a heap that keeps growing past it is collected.

Soundness
  Pacing only.

Failure modes
  A program may hold up to 16 MB of garbage cycles before its first collection. Embedders that call JS_SetGCThreshold keep their value.

--- a/quickjs.c
+++ b/quickjs.c
@@ -3373,14 +3373,9 @@
                 js_drc_reconcile(rt);
                 if (rt->malloc_state.malloc_size + size <=
                     rt->malloc_gc_threshold) {
-                    /* A reconcile is not a collection: it must not count as an unproductive one, or the threshold ratchets up by a factor of
-                       five each time the parked values are what grew the heap and cyclic garbage is never collected. */
+                    /* A reconcile is not a collection: the threshold stays where the last collection put it (its result plus the growth step).
+                       Moving it up with the heap, as every rearm did, made it follow the uncollected cyclic garbage and never be reached. */
                     gc_trig[1]++;
-                    {
-                        size_t step_ = rt->malloc_state.malloc_size >> 1;
-
-                        rt->malloc_gc_threshold = rt->malloc_state.malloc_size + (step_ < GC_MIN_STEP ? GC_MIN_STEP : step_);
-                    }
                     return;
                 }
             }
@@ -4267,7 +4262,7 @@
     rt->malloc_state = ms;
     rt->json_lazy_enabled = QJS_JSON_LAZY_DEFAULT;
     js_arena_init(rt);
-    rt->malloc_gc_threshold = 256 * 1024;
+    rt->malloc_gc_threshold = GC_MIN_STEP;
     rt->gc_pace_streak_cap = JS_GC_PACE_STREAK_DEFAULT;
     rt->gc_cyc_empty_streak = 0;
 
